  ('014418e3-7100-5436-84aa-bf6d03bd8e54', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-narrative-writing'), null, 'easy',
   $q$The writer wants to use dialogue in sentence 8. Which revision does this best?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Have you tried the grocery store?\" he asked me with a confused look.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"gives-line-to-wrong-speaker"},{"text":"I shook my head no, and he looked at the floor for a while.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"no-dialogue"},{"text":"\"Sorry,\" I said, nodding at the empty rack by the door. \"That man just took the last one.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"I told him that unfortunately we were completely out of snow shovels.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"summary-not-dialogue"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Sorry," I said, nodding at the empty rack by the door. "That man just took the last one."$q$, $q$The correct choice lets the narrator speak and points to the empty rack, connecting to sentence 6. The first choice still summarizes the answer instead of giving the narrator's words.$q$, 'draft', '0263af8c-9911-59cf-b483-df6aaced16f9')
