  ('82c53c08-0f19-5fe0-a78a-e4031064d887', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-narrative-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence 17 as a conclusion that reflects on the experience and both plot lines?$q$, $q$[{"text":"When he finally looked up, Kofi asked if we could come back tomorrow, and I realized the clouds had made the comet worth more.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Comets are made of ice and dust, and their tails always point away from the sun as they travel.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"generic-fact-ending"},{"text":"Ines wrote a report about the night for the club newsletter, and it was printed the following week.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ends-on-minor-thread"},{"text":"The comet was green and had a tail, and it was in the western sky where the forecast had said it would be.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-situation"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$When he finally looked up, Kofi asked if we could come back tomorrow, and I realized the clouds had made the comet worth more.$q$, $q$The correct choice resolves Kofi's thread (he now wants to return) and reflects on how the wait gave the sighting its value. The newsletter choice ends on a side detail and offers no reflection.$q$, 'draft', '889c5e8c-d2ae-54ab-bcb8-2938fb757d75')
